The '''Nine Lords' War''' (九子奪嫡, ''jiǔ zǐ duó dí'') refers to the political struggle among nine of the late-reign sons of [[Kangxi Emperor|Emperor Kangxi]] of the [[Qing dynasty]] over succession to the [[Imperial throne of China|imperial throne]].<ref>{{cite book|title=清史稿|author=趙爾巽|year=1928}}</ref> The conflict ended with the accession of [[Yongzheng Emperor|Yinzhen, the fourth prince]] (皇四子胤禛).<ref name="qingshi" />

== Background ==

The [[Kangxi Emperor]] reigned for sixty-one years. Early in his reign he designated his second son, [[Yinreng]], as [[Crown Prince]]. Owing to the expanding influence of the [[Crown Prince's faction]] and concerns over Yinreng's personal conduct, Kangxi deposed the Crown Prince in the forty-seventh year of his reign (1708).<ref>{{cite book|title=康熙朝實錄|year=1731}}</ref>

